{
  "title": "Transient Synovitis of Hip",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4030/transient-synovitis-of-hip",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 13 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Transient Synovitis of Hip is inflammation of the synovium and a common cause of hip pain in pediatric patients that must be differentiated from septic arthritis of the hip.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is one of exclusion and can be suspected in a patient with hip pain with low CRP and near normal synovial WBC count.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually anti-inflammatories and observation given self-limiting nature.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**most common cause of hip pain in the pediatric population**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**3% of children between 3-10yo**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**recurrence rate is as high as 20%**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common in children aged **4-8 years old**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "male-to-female ratio is 2:1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can affect any major joint but most commonly affects the hip joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**the exact cause of transient synovitis is largely unknown**, however, may be related to",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "viral infection (upper respiratory)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bacterial infection (**poststreptococcal toxic synovitis**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "trauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "higher interferon concentration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "allergic reaction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "non-specific inflammation and hypertrophy of the synovial lining/membrane",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recent upper respiratory infection or trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mild or absent fever",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "acute or **insidious onset of groin/thigh pain**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "refusal to bear weight on the affected extremity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "usually improves during the day (child can walk with a limp later in the day)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "muscle spasms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hip presents in flexion, abduction, and external rotation (**position with least amount of intracapsular pressure**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "usually does not have a toxic appearance",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "mild to moderate **restriction of hip internal rotation** is the most sensitive range-of-motion restriction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "a painless arc of motion is more likely synovitis rather than septic arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "toe-walking, cavus foot, or clawing of the toes may suggest a neurological cause of limp",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "log-rolling leg can detect involuntary muscle guarding",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "non-tender motion of lumbar spine and ipsilateral knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4030/images/normal_ap_pelvis.jpg",
                  "caption": "Normal radiograph of a pediatric pelvis"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP, lateral or frog leg hip views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "optional radiographs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**spine films**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually normal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasonography",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "history and physical examination suspicious for septic arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "accurate for detecting intracapsular fluid/effusion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4030/images/ultrasound_left_hip.jpg",
                      "caption": "Ultrasound of a left pediatric hip without an effusion"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may show synovial membrane thickening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "sensitivity/specificity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**difficult to distinguish transient synovitis from septic arthritis, but infection less likely if effusion absent**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "suspicion for myositis or osteomyelitis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "significantly elevated lab values",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Serum labs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "WBC may be slightly elevated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**CRP < 20 mg/l**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**most important factor to RULE OUT septic arthritis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ESR usually less than 20 mm/h",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Invasive studies",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "synovial fluid aspiration if concern for septic arthritis based on clinical judgment or Kocher criteria",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "assume it is septic arthritis if synovial WBC is >50,000",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Hip septic arthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Osteomyelitis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "SCFE",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDS and close observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "low clinical suspicion of septic arthritis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "treat the patient with IV or PO NSAIDS and observe over 24 hours",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "minimize walking for 24 hours",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "consider traction to enforce rest",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if symptoms improve with NSAIDS, more likely to be transient synovitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "symptom resolution in under 1 week from the date of presentation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence ~ 20%**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Legg-Calve-Perthes**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "reported as 0-10% incidence however his is controversial as most series show no long term sequelae",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Natural history of disease",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually benign",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**marked improvement, usually in 24-48 hours**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "complete resolution of symptoms will usually occur in 1-2 weeks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
